No. In development, Strict Mode intentionally runs an extra **setup → cleanup → setup** cycle as a stress test for your Effect; production normally performs setup once on mount. [1][3]

Write the Effect so its cleanup fully undoes its setup—for example, disconnect the connection created by that setup: [1][3]

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const connection = createConnection(serverUrl, roomId);
  connection.connect();

  return () => connection.disconnect();
}, [roomId]);
```

The user should not be able to distinguish between a single setup and the development-only **setup → cleanup → setup** sequence. [3]

