`memo` only skips re-rendering when all props are the same as on the previous render.[1][4] An `options` object created during every parent render is always a new value, so it breaks memoization and the child re-renders.[2][4]

Memoize the object with `useMemo` and include its dependencies:

```js
const options = useMemo(
  () => ({ /* options */ }),
  [/* values used to create options */]
);

return <MemoizedChild options={options} />;
```

The dependency array prevents unnecessary recalculation while its dependencies remain unchanged; if a dependency changes every render, remove or memoize that dependency too.[5]

